acceptance_criteria:
Contextual inspector

Selected-agent inspection exposes:

- identity;
- trusted lifecycle;
- exact trusted activity;
- trusted reason when present;
- freshness/last-known qualification where applicable.

Do not add statistics, history, tabs, task/provider controls, or model/token/cost/productivity information.

Availability hierarchy

Availability remains separate from lifecycle and truthfully represents:

- connecting without trusted state;
- connected/synchronized;
- synchronizing with retained state;
- disconnected with retained state;
- disconnected without trusted data.

Normal composition

At 1100 × 760:

- office remains dominant;
- availability is concise;
- contextual inspection uses side placement;
- selector remains compact;
- application chrome does not become a dashboard-card grid.

Minimum composition

At 760 × 540:

- single-column composition;
- readable fixed office;
- no horizontal page scrolling;
- compact selector remains reachable;
- immediate selected name + trusted lifecycle feedback is available near
the visible office/selection surface;
- full inspector is reachable below through vertical document scrolling.
